GAL16V8
C128MMU2

A0  A1  A2  A3  RW  D0  D1  D6  D7  GND
NC  NC  NC  NC  D0X D6X NC  NC  NC  VCC

; Data remap for the second 8722 MMU (U2) on the C128DCR MMU riser.
; Device: Microchip ATF16V8B (GAL16V8 compatible), complex mode.
;
; D6X -> U2 D6: CPU D6 at $xxx5 (MCR), $xxx7 (P0L), $xxx9 (P1L);
;               CPU D7 everywhere else, so U2's bank bit 6 follows the
;               CPU's 256K bank bit 7 (CR, PCRs, RCR, $FF00 LCR).
; D0X -> U2 D0: CPU D1 at $xxx8 / $xxxA (P0H / P1H bank pointers);
;               CPU D0 everywhere else.
; Both outputs drive only while R/W is low (a write); during reads they
; are off, so U2 never fights them.
;
; Pass-D6 addresses (A3..A0): 0101, 0111 -> /A3*A2*A0 ; 1001 -> A3*/A2*/A1*A0
; Their complement:           /A0 + /A3*/A2 + A3*A2 + A3*A1

D6X.T = D6 * /A3 * A2 * A0
      + D6 * A3 * /A2 * /A1 * A0
      + D7 * /A0
      + D7 * /A3 * /A2
      + D7 * A3 * A2
      + D7 * A3 * A1
D6X.E = /RW

D0X.T = D1 * A3 * /A2 * /A0
      + D0 * /A3
      + D0 * A2
      + D0 * A0
D0X.E = /RW

DESCRIPTION

C128DCR MMU riser, second-MMU data remap.  After ytmytm/c128-mmu-256k-exp
(GAL22V10 equations), with two changes: P0L/P1L ($xxx7/$xxx9) are passed
unremapped so both MMUs hold the same relocation pages, and the outputs are
3-stated during reads.  Build: galasm riser.pld -> riser.jed.
